# Line endings are content here, not formatting.
#
# `sqlx` records a checksum of each migration's bytes and refuses to run against
# a database whose recorded checksum differs. Without this file the working tree
# gets CRLF on Windows and LF on Linux, so the same commit produces two
# different checksums — and whichever machine migrated first locks every other
# one out with "migration 1 was previously applied but has been modified".
#
# Caught by a container refusing to start against a database a Windows checkout
# had already migrated. The same hazard applies to anything hashed or signed, so
# the rule is the whole tree rather than just `migrations/`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
